course: dictionary
lesson: 4480
title: Hartebeest: a grassland antelope
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A hartebeest is a large African antelope. It has a long face, a sloping back and curved horns, and it lives on grassy plains. When you meet this word, look for clues in the text that tell you what kind of animal it is.
explain: Kipling's story gives you a clue: «The Giraffe, the Zebra, the Eland, the Koodoo (kudu) and the Hartebeest lived there». The hartebeest lives with other animals on the High Veldt. Eland and kudu are also African antelopes, so the hartebeest belongs to that same family.
explain: A science lesson on the savanna gives another clue: the food chain. Hartebeest eat grass, and lions, leopards and hyenas hunt them. If an animal eats grass and is hunted by big predators, you know it is prey in the food chain.
fact: A hartebeest is a large African antelope.
fact: It has a long face, a sloping back and curved horns.
fact: Hartebeest live on grassy plains, such as the savanna.
fact: Hartebeest eat grass, and lions, leopards and hyenas hunt them.
fact: The plural of hartebeest is hartebeest or hartebeests.
exercise: What is a hartebeest? | A small grey bird that sings at dawn | A type of tall tree | *A large African antelope with a long face and curved horns | A sea fish with sharp teeth
exercise: In Kipling's story, the hartebeest lives on the High Veldt. What kind of place is that? | A frozen ice field | *A grassy plain | A dark cave under a mountain | A coral reef in the sea
exercise: Lions, leopards and hyenas hunt hartebeest. What does this tell you about hartebeest in the food chain? | *They are prey, eaten by other animals | They live only in the sea | They never eat grass | They are the top hunter of the savanna
test: The eland and the kudu in Kipling's story are also what kind of animal? | *African antelopes | Birds | Lions | Hyenas
test: Which sentence from the story tells you the animals were the same colour? | *«were all "sandy-yellow-brownish all over"» | «and the Leopard hunts them» | «High Veldt» are the same colour | «The Giraffe, the Zebra, the Eland, the Koodoo (kudu) and the Hartebeest lived there»
exam: Which sentence describes a hartebeest correctly? | *A hartebeest is a large African antelope with curved horns | A hartebeest is a tall tree with long leaves | A hartebeest is a fish that swims in the sea | A hartebeest is a small bird that flies over the plains
